@M_KOJO_IRAI_UNIQUE_201_K102(ROLE, SCENE, CLIENT_ID)
#DIMS ROLE     ;キャラの立場、依頼者かそうでないか
#DIMS SCENE    ;セリフの表示されるタイミング
#DIM  CLIENT_ID;依頼者IDだけ抜き出したもの
;--------------------------------------------------
;RETURN 0 の部分は共通の口上が表示されます
;依頼ごとの口上を表示する部分は RETURN 0 を RETURN 1 にしてください
;--------------------------------------------------
SELECTCASE SCENE
CASE "依頼提示時"
	PRINTFORML 「Danmaku? It's a non-lethal, aerial magic shootout regulated by the Spell Card Rules.」
	PRINTFORML 「It is akin to lethal combat, except that characters have【Lives】, which dictate if they're still in or not.」
	PRINTFORML 「Furthermore, any non-Danmaku based weaponry is banned, so it's best to level your Danmaku first.」
    PRINTFORML 「The premise is to take out your opponent's lives before they take out yours.」
    PRINTL
	PRINTFORML 「You can practice in any large open area, so be sure to do so.」
	PRINTFORML 「You'll be sometimes challenged by ruffians when either heading out or in a hostile area.」
	PRINTL
	PRINTFORML 「The idea is to attack the enemy and survive against your enemy's attacks by dodging.」
	PRINTFORML 「Each bullet that lands will deal damage to a Touhou's HP.」
	PRINTFORML 「You can use spell cards to go for heavy damage or even take out a Touhou's【Life】, just be careful of your MP.」
	RETURN 1
CASE "Losing Lives"
    PRINTFORML 「When a combatant run out of hit points in a Danmaku battle, they'll lose a life.」
    PRINTFORML 「A Pichuun/Biu sound will notify you that you have been hit, if you lost a life.」
    PRINTFORML 「Losing all of your lives will make you lose the match, so be sure to not be too careless.」
    PRINTFORML 「Lose all of the enemy's lives, and they'll be out of the battle.」
CASE "Losing"
    PRINTFORML 「When you lose all lives or willingly surrender, that means you have lost the match.」
    PRINTFORML 「You will gain much less experience losing than if you had won.」
    PRINTFORML 「No matter what happens during a Danmaku match, any MP used will not automatically recover after the match.」
CASE "Winning"
    PRINTFORML 「When your enemy loses all lives, that means you have won.」
    PRINTFORML 「You will gain a hefty amount of experience and perhaps a scroll if they had one.」
    PRINTFORML 「No matter what happens during a Danmaku match, any MP used will not automatically recover after the match.」
CASE "Misses"
    CALL SHOW_IRAI_MESSAGE(102, 202, "Misses")
CASE "Dodged Hits"
    CALL SHOW_IRAI_MESSAGE(102, 202, "Dodged Hits")
CASE "Your Turn"
    CALL SHOW_IRAI_MESSAGE(102, 202, "Your Turn")
CASE "依頼非受託時"
	PRINTDATAL
		DATAFORM 「You don't have to come with me, though you're better off if you do.」
	ENDDATA
	RETURN 1
CASE "依頼受託時"
	PRINTDATAW
		DATAFORM 「Thank you. I know you probably need me to guide you.」
	ENDDATA
    IF !GETBIT(TALENT:MASTER:ESP,0)
	PRINTL
	PRINTFORMW 「Oh, and do you not know how to use Danmaku?」
	PRINTFORMW 「Ah, as an Outsider, Danmaku is something that is learned, however most Gensokyan natives will already know how to Danmaku.」
	PRINTFORMW 「I can easily give you the ability since you'll need it to continue.」
    PRINTFORMW 「Keep in mind that a character with Danmaku can be worse than one without if there's not enough training.」
    SETBIT TALENT:MASTER:ESP, 0
    MAXBASE:MASTER:7 = MAX(MAXBASE:MASTER:7,100)
    BASE:MASTER:7 = MAXBASE:MASTER:7
    CALL COLORMESSAGE(@"You now have 【Youjutsu: Danmaku】", C_AQUA,2)
    ENDIF
	RETURN 1
CASE "依頼確認時"
	RETURN 1
CASE "依頼破棄時"
	RETURN 1
CASE "依頼実行直前"
    RETURN 0
CASE "依頼実行直後"
	RETURN 0
CASE "成功報告時"
;報酬： 
	RETURN 1
CASE "失敗報告時"
	PRINTDATAL
		DATAFORM 「Ah, you can always do another then.」
	ENDDATA
	RETURN 1
	;IF !RESULT
	;	PRINTFORML
CASE "依頼報告不要"
	RETURN 0
ENDSELECT

@M_KOJO_IRAI_UNIQUE_202_K102(ROLE, SCENE, CLIENT_ID)
#DIMS ROLE     ;キャラの立場、依頼者かそうでないか
#DIMS SCENE    ;セリフの表示されるタイミング
#DIM  CLIENT_ID;依頼者IDだけ抜き出したもの
;--------------------------------------------------
;RETURN 0 の部分は共通の口上が表示されます
;依頼ごとの口上を表示する部分は RETURN 0 を RETURN 1 にしてください
;--------------------------------------------------
SELECTCASE SCENE
CASE "依頼提示時"
	PRINTFORML 「Lethal Combat may seem a little daunting to new residents at first, however a few simple guidelines will have you ready to repel attacks and hold ground like a pro.」
	PRINTFORML 「In every gunfight there is one very important lifesaving rule to remember:」
    FONTBOLD
	PRINTFORML 「Always use whatever cover is available!」
    FONTREGULAR
    PRINTFORML 「The premise is to take out your opponent's team before they take out your team.」
    PRINTFORML 「Any damage you inflict will damage the opponent's body. If death is enabled, you could even kill them if you destroy one of their essential parts.」
    PRINTL
	PRINTFORML 「Your skills and your weapon determine your success the most.」
	PRINTFORML 「You may have a good weapon, but without the skills to show for it, you won't be able to hit the broad side of a barn.」
	PRINTFORML 「Conversely, if you are a good shot but only have a .22LR pistol, you won't be killing anything any time soon.」
	PRINTFORML 「It is essential to train up your skill that your weapon corresponds to.」
	PRINTFORML 「Your skills and your weapon determine your success the most.」
	PRINTFORML 「Danmaku corresponds to the Danmaku Skill, Firearms are helped with the shooting skill, and Melee weapons are enhanced with the Melee skill.」
	PRINTFORML 「Being great at one combat stat (Danmaku, Shooting or Melee) is better than being decent at all three.」
    PRINTL
	PRINTFORML 「You can practice in any large open area, so be sure to do so.」
	PRINTFORML 「You'll be sometimes challenged by ruffians when either heading out or in a hostile area.」
	PRINTL
	PRINTFORML 「The idea is to attack the enemy and survive against your enemy's attacks by dodging and taking cover.」
	PRINTFORML 「Each hit that lands will deal damage to a Touhou's STA and damage some of their body parts.」
	PRINTFORML 「The last team who stands wins.」
	RETURN 1
CASE "Out of HP"
    PRINTFORML 「When a combatant run out of Stamina in a Lethal battle, they'll will faint.」
    PRINTFORML 「You will instantly lose if you faint, so be sure to not be too careless.」
CASE "Losing"
    PRINTFORML 「When you faint or willingly surrender, that means you have lost the match.」
    PRINTFORML 「You will gain much less experience losing than if you had won.」
    PRINTFORML 「No matter what happens during Lethal Combat, any wounds afflicted will stay and will need to be tended.」
CASE "Winning"
    PRINTFORML 「When your enemy loses all lives, that means you have won.」
    PRINTFORML 「You will gain a hefty amount of experience and perhaps a scroll if they had one.」
    PRINTFORML 「No matter what happens during Lethal Combat, any wounds afflicted will stay and will need to be tended.」
CASE "Misses"
    PRINTFORML 「When a character misses a shot, no damage will be dealt to the recipient.」
CASE "Dodged Hits"
    PRINTFORML 「When a character dodges a shot, that means the bullet was supposed to land, but the recipient dodged it.」
    PRINTFORML 「Dodged bullets act like missed ones and result in no damage.」
CASE "Your Turn"
    PRINTFORML 「The attack priority is shown on the top, which shows who's turn it is, who will go next, as well as implying who has already acted within the turn.」
    PRINTFORML 「Turns are self explanatory. The only catch here is that there is a 150 turn ultimatum that will forcefully end the fight with no winner.」
    PRINTFORML 「This is usually not hit unless there's ridiculous circumstances such as low accuracy weapons, or incompetent shooters vs incompetent shooters.」
    PRINTL
    PRINTFORML 「You can %TW_PORT_STR(@"Attack",1)%normally, or attack precisely. Attacking normally will target a random body part, but most likely you will end up hitting the torso.」
    PRINTFORML 「%TW_PORT_STR(@"Precise Shot",1)% can be used to specifically target a body part in case you don't want to kill the target, or if you're aiming at the target's head.」
    PRINTFORML 「%TW_PORT_STR(@"Skills",1)%allows you to use a spell card that you have in your loadout, as well as using Danmaku items during battle.」
    PRINTFORML 「%TW_PORT_STR(@"Taking",1)%cover will put you in a random cover piece which can stop some rounds.」
    PRINTFORML 「%TW_PORT_STR(@"Tending",1)%wounds will tend all of your current wounds and give you 500 STA, but at the cost of your turn.」
    PRINTFORML 「%TW_PORT_STR(@"Reloading",1)%will use your turn to replenish all ammunition in your magazine.」
    PRINTFORML 「%TW_PORT_STR(@"Switch Weapon",1)%will allow you to switch your weapon to another weapon that you already own.」
    PRINTFORML 「%TW_PORT_STR(@"Retreating",1)%ends the fight if you are more powerful than the enemy, else there's a chance that you might not escape.」
    PRINTFORML 「%TW_PORT_STR(@"Subdue",1)%will try to get the enemy to surrender to you. This is based off your %TW_PORT_STR("Speech",1)%.」
    PRINTFORML 「%TW_PORT_STR(@"Submitting",1)%ends the fight, but leaves you getting raped or robbed, and ends your day immediately.」
    PRINTFORML 「%TW_PORT_STR(@"NPC Direct Control",1)%allows you to take control of any allied non-playable characters in the fight. When off, you will only control yourself.」
CASE "Armor"
    PRINTFORML 「Armor is used to protect body parts from being damaged and to decrease the amount of damage done to Stamina and the body.」
    PRINTFORML
    PRINTFORML 「Armors have 3 main stats:」
    PRINTFORML 「%BREAKENG(@"Armor Strength: How much penetration a weapon will need to have to inflict to fully penetrate the armor and deal full damage. If a gun has a pen of 3 hits a body part protected by an armor rated PM 13, damage will be dramatically reduced. Armor strength is in the European VPAM standard. PM 1 is equal to 1 pen.")%」
    PRINTFORML 「%BREAKENG(@"Armor Durability: Indicates how much damage the armor can take (in kJ) before breaking. As armor degrades, it's effective strength will drastically go down until it either breaks or becomes useless.")%」
    PRINTFORML 「%BREAKENG(@"Armor Coverage: Shows which part of the body will be protected by the armor.")%」
    PRINTL
    PRINTFORML Armor can be countered by using armor-piercing rounds or weapons with higher penetration.
CASE "依頼非受託時"
	PRINTDATAL
		DATAFORM 「You don't have to come with me, though you're better off if you do.」
	ENDDATA
	RETURN 1
CASE "依頼受託時"
	RETURN 1
CASE "依頼確認時"
	RETURN 1
CASE "依頼破棄時"
	RETURN 1
CASE "依頼実行直前"
	RETURN 0
CASE "依頼実行直後"
	RETURN 0
CASE "成功報告時"
;報酬： 
	RETURN 1
CASE "失敗報告時"
	PRINTDATAL
		DATAFORM 「Ah, you can always do another then.」
	ENDDATA
	RETURN 1
	;IF !RESULT
	;	PRINTFORML
CASE "依頼報告不要"
	RETURN 0
ENDSELECT

@M_KOJO_IRAI_UNIQUE_203_K102(ROLE, SCENE, CLIENT_ID)
#DIMS ROLE     ;キャラの立場、依頼者かそうでないか
#DIMS SCENE    ;セリフの表示されるタイミング
#DIM  CLIENT_ID;依頼者IDだけ抜き出したもの
;--------------------------------------------------
;RETURN 0 の部分は共通の口上が表示されます
;依頼ごとの口上を表示する部分は RETURN 0 を RETURN 1 にしてください
;--------------------------------------------------
SELECTCASE SCENE
CASE "依頼提示時"
	PRINTFORML 「Health in this world uses a Hediff system where each wound is unique as it's given a damage type, severity, and tags that show where it came from.」
	PRINTFORML 「Each injury affects a different part of the characters' well being, and can be found under a character's Health tab.」
	PRINTFORML 「Different weapons cause different types of injuries. For example, a mace will crush, a longsword will cut, and fire will burn.」
	PRINTFORML 「The type of injury impacts the amount of pain it causes, the rate of bleeding, and the chance of infection」
	PRINTFORML 「Injuries affect the efficiency of actions and their viability of parts.」
	PRINTL
	PRINTFORML 「For this tutorial, you'll be damaged enough to start bleeding.」
	PRINTFORML 「You'll need to tend to the injury using the【Doctoring】command immediately, or else you might bleed to death.」
	RETURN 1
CASE "Tending"
    PRINTFORML 「The only way for a part to heal HP is with time, but tending will increase it's effectiveness immensely.」
    PRINTFORML 「Tending wounds will also make it less likely for a wound infection to happen and stops bleeding.」
	PRINTL
	PRINTFORML 「Tended wounds have quality, which is determined by your medical skill and medicine used for tending.」
	PRINTFORML 「Higher quality tending makes wounds heal faster.」
CASE "Bleeding"
    PRINTFORML 「Bleeding is a common occurrence from certain damage types.」
    PRINTFORML 「While an injury is bleeding, the character will gain blood loss, scaling with the wound and amount of wounds.」
    PRINTFORML 「If a character has no more blood, they will instantly die, with the kill credited to those who fought the Touhou last」
	PRINTFORML 「It's best to stop bleeding as soon as possible if you want to stay alive.」
CASE "依頼非受託時"
	PRINTDATAL
		DATAFORM 「You don't have to come with me, though you're better off if you do.」
	ENDDATA
	RETURN 1
CASE "依頼受託時"
	PRINTFORMDW You feel a sudden pain in your chest.
	PRINTFORMW 「Use the medkits that I gave you to tend to the wound using the 【Doctoring】 menu.」
	CALL GET_ITEM("FirstAidKit",3,2)
	CALLF DamageBodyPart(MASTER,40,TALENT:MASTER:40 ? 1000 # 500,3,102,"Tutorial Wound")
	RETURN 1
CASE "依頼確認時"
	RETURN 1
CASE "依頼破棄時"
	RETURN 1
CASE "依頼実行直前"
	RETURN 0
CASE "依頼実行直後"
	RETURN 0
CASE "成功報告時"
;報酬： 
	RETURN 1
CASE "失敗報告時"
	PRINTDATAL
		DATAFORM 「Ah, you can always do another then.」
	ENDDATA
	RETURN 1
	;IF !RESULT
	;	PRINTFORML
CASE "依頼報告不要"
	RETURN 0
ENDSELECT